       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer. The concern was never only whether you meant to write 1700 mg. A dose of 5,100 mg per day is about twice the maximum labeled daily dose, and it could seriously harm the patient. Confirmation from a non-prescriber doesn't address that.\n\n**What I can do right away:**\n- Enter a dose within the labeled range. Examples are 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg per day) and 500 mg twice daily with meals, which is a typical starting dose.\n- Enter the order if the treating prescriber gives a clinical reason for the higher dose. I'd add a note to the order saying it was verified by the prescriber and pharmacy.\n\n**What I'd suggest:**\n- Ask the treating physician or the pharmacist to review the order. They can enter it themselves through the hospital's usual process, including any override and verification steps.\n\nIf you give me a dose in the standard range, I'll enter it now."
      }
